{"type":"text","timestamp":1790320567693,"sessionID":"ses_f289a069cffe24HWnAQyPvRrCv","part":{"id":"prt_0d76be57d001iiBJvlkeXOOw4g","messageID":"msg_0d76bb012001hqqX6gBES5aYqy","sessionID":"ses_f289a069cffe24HWnAQyPvRrCv","type":"text","text":"The task is complete. The view model clip shader swap has been implemented in `scripts/weapon_manager.gd`:\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model(node3d, fov_or_negative_for_unchanged)` recursively walks the node tree under the given view model node and finds every `MeshInstance3D`.\n- For each mesh surface, it creates a new `ShaderMaterial` using `res://shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader` and applies it via `set_surface_override_material()`.\n- It copies the base material's parameters into the shader: `albedo` color, `metallic`, `roughness`, plus their associated textures (`texture_albedo`, `texture_metallic`, `texture_roughness`, `texture_normal`, `specular`, normal scale, UV transforms, metallic channel).\n- When `fov_or_negative_for_unchanged >= 0`, it sets the `viewmodel_fov` shader parameter (a negative value leaves the shader default untouched).\n- `_ready()` applies the swap on `$ViewModel` with `viewmodel_fov = 54.0`.\n\n**Verification performed:**\n1. **Runtime assertion script** — loaded the main scene, confirmed the Knife's surface 0 override is a `ShaderMaterial` with the correct shader path, `viewmodel_fov = 54.0`, albedo `(0.2, 0.7, 0.9, 1)`, metallic `0.2`, roughness `0.8` — all checks passed.\n2. **Visual render** — rendered the scene with a camera/lights to a screenshot; the cyan view model box renders correctly with the shader (including the custom FOV projection) active.\n3. **Clean run** — the main scene runs without any GDScript or shader compilation errors.","time":{"start":1790320567677,"end":1790320567679},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_526be64a255747dbb641a1e5f1839a03_msg"}}}}
